# =============================================================================
# oshal-apps — app-package store.
#
# This repo ships PRODUCT CODE only. User data (career_db.json, resumes, crm.db,
# generated application packets) is per-user runtime state and lives outside git,
# in the per-user encrypted store / persistent volume. Nothing here should ever
# capture a real person's profile, documents, or credentials.
# =============================================================================

# Compiled Python bytecode — build artifacts, regenerated on every run.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Node / build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets and environment. Never commit a real .env; ship .env.example instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
**/.env
**/.env.*
secrets.json
**/secrets.json
*service-account*.json
google-credentials*.json

# Local databases and generated user state. career_db.json is a REAL PERSON'S
# profile (built from their uploaded resume) and crm.db holds their pipeline —
# both are runtime data, never product code.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
career_db.json
**/career_db.json
_career-db/
**/_career-db/
applications/
**/applications/

# Generated application packets (resumes/cover letters carry PII)
*.pdf.tmp
.apply-work/

# Cert/key material
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# Screenshots and local capture debris — these have repeatedly turned out to contain
# real faces, real account balances, and filled-in application forms.
#
# Deliberately matched by NAME, not by extension. A blanket `*.png` would also have
# swallowed 21 legitimate product assets (dnd/data/maps + dnd/data/tokens), which is
# the same over-broad-rule mistake that would have broken TTS in the core scrub:
# ignore what the debris IS called, not every file of that type.
Screenshot*.png
Screenshot*.jpg
Screen?Shot*.png
screenshot-*.png
screen-capture-*.png
*-capture-*.png
_walkthrough-shots/
_screenshots/

# Logs, temp, OS/editor junk
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Local handover / session notes
**/HANDOVER.md
